  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 933 PM MDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nThe high pressure that has been centered overhead the past few days \nis starting to flatten out and nudge to our south. This puts us in \nwesterly flow, which happens to be where the moisture is residing. \nThis uptick in moisture will result in more showers and storms \nacross the area tomorrow and following days. This initial moisture \nwill be mainly in the midlevels leaving the lower levels rather dry \nstill. This will make it difficult for measurable rainfall and \nincrease the potential for gusty outflow winds upwards of 45 mph or \nhigher. With the lack of forcing showers will develop over the high \nterrain before moving over the valleys. Coverage looks to gradually \nincrease each day early next week, but the better chances appear\nto be mid to late week. Models are hinting at a few troughs in the\nregion and slightly deeper mositure. With the high nudging south\nalong with the increase in showers and clouds temperatures are \nexpected to start cooling each day through the forecast period.",
